From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:46:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Fail a style sheet whose body ends with a network
 error

The style sheet loader parsed and applied whatever part of a body it had
received when the body ended with a network error, and fired `load`. When
the body is fully read with a failure, the linked resource is processed
with success set to false, so no style sheet applies and `error` fires.
Do that for a `link` and for an `@import`: as for a status that is not ok,
Servo gives the link, or the import rule, an empty style sheet.

Net reports a body cut short by the connection as complete today, so the
cut-short cases of the new test are expected to fail until it reports it
as a network error.

Validation: New test `tests/wpt/mozilla/tests/mozilla/stylesheet-network-error.html`: its decode error cases pass; its cut-short cases are expected to fail until `net: End a body cut short by the connection with a network error`, and pass with it.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent wrote this patch and its test following docs/fetch-p4a-truncated-body-audit-2026-10-22.md in the workspace, and applied an independent review's findings)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
